# Design variants isolation

Owners compare designs via a password gate and hub at `/`. Eventually one variant wins; the others are removed.

## Variants

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `/` | Hub only (chooser) — not a design variant |
| `/standard/` | Current marketing site design |
| `/experimental/` | Alternate design (may be stub) |
| `/archivio/` | Old photos/texts archive |

## Isolation (do not entangle)

- Each variant owns its **route tree** and **chrome** (layouts, headers, styles, variant-specific components).
- Do **not** share layouts or UI components across variants (no parent layout that wraps more than one variant’s chrome).
- Do **not** add cross-links between variants in nav/footer; the **hub** is the only crossroads.
- **Allowed shared code** (survives whichever wins): gate/hub, `content.ts` / archive data, `static/` assets, and the tiny hub back-arrow helper.
- When a design wins: delete the other variant folders and their components; re-point or remove hub/gate as needed — no cross-variant refactor.

## Hub back arrow

- All three variants show the same subtle top-left control back to `/` (hub).
- Prefer one small shared component (e.g. `HubBack`); keep it trivial to keep or inline later.
